WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.359 --> 00:00:03.023
- So, we tried these before.

00:00:04.013 --> 00:00:04.569
- Delicious.

00:00:04.569 --> 00:00:06.357
- But we didn't really
know you were supposed

00:00:06.357 --> 00:00:07.242
to put stuff in them.

00:00:07.242 --> 00:00:08.684
- There's nothing inside.

00:00:08.684 --> 00:00:11.602
- This time we're going
to put stuff in them.

00:00:13.322 --> 00:00:15.513
We're probably still gonna mess it up.

00:00:16.847 --> 00:00:18.920
- There's just nothing that looks like any

00:00:18.920 --> 00:00:20.179
of these things in America.

00:00:20.179 --> 00:00:22.069
- This is like a little
boat for your food.

00:00:22.069 --> 00:00:23.288
- These are so cute.

00:00:23.288 --> 00:00:25.238
- You put some of this stuff in it.

00:00:25.238 --> 00:00:26.396
- Moon beams.

00:00:26.396 --> 00:00:27.819
- [Girl in Jean Jacket] You
got a little bit of this.

00:00:27.819 --> 00:00:29.139
- Tamarind sauce.

00:00:29.139 --> 00:00:30.230
- [Girl in Jean Jacket] The final part is

00:00:30.230 --> 00:00:31.652
like a big old dip.

00:00:31.652 --> 00:00:32.729
- Your flavored water.

00:00:32.729 --> 00:00:34.050
- Let's get to business.

00:00:34.050 --> 00:00:36.565
- (pani puri crunching)
Oh, my God. Oh, my God.

00:00:36.565 --> 00:00:37.856
- I do get the feeling
you're supposed to take it

00:00:37.856 --> 00:00:39.426
all in one bite.

00:00:40.375 --> 00:00:42.000
It's like crazy (beep) good.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:43.585
- The sauces are magical.

00:00:43.585 --> 00:00:45.718
- Spicy, sweet, earthy.

00:00:45.718 --> 00:00:47.425
- Oh, no. I'm sorry, little pillow.

00:00:47.425 --> 00:00:49.050
- It's like a savory Gusher.

00:00:49.050 --> 00:00:50.411
- It's like filling up
a pita with something.

00:00:50.411 --> 00:00:53.096
- If this is the way pani
puri is supposed to be eaten,

00:00:53.096 --> 00:00:54.605
is that how you say it?

00:00:54.755 --> 00:00:56.900
(laughs) Probably saying it incorrectly.

00:00:57.823 --> 00:00:59.266
Pani puri, really?

00:00:59.266 --> 00:00:59.689
- [Man behind Camera] I don't know.

00:00:59.689 --> 00:01:00.543
- Oh, God.

00:01:00.543 --> 00:01:03.123
- I can't really think of an
American equivalent for this.

00:01:03.123 --> 00:01:05.012
- And that's a problem, America.

00:01:05.012 --> 00:01:07.371
We need to step our (beep) game up.

